      "difficulty_reason": "The proof converts negative assumptions into codirected compact-saturated approximation families, uses spectral/Scott-domain compactness to choose a common finite approximation, and reduces positive output properties to the complete finite conjunction fragment. The full neutral-fragment typing completeness induction and logical normal-form/spectral support are retained, rather than assumed away. This is a non-routine domain-theoretic logical completeness construction, supporting H2 as one main result.",
